# Implementation Plan — Sprint-003A: Browser Foundation

Implement the backend/infrastructure **Browser Foundation Engine** (`src/browser/`) to serve as the core service layer for future Browser UI components (Sprint-003B).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> According to explicit constraints, **NO UI widgets** (`QWebEngineView`, `BrowserPanel`, Address Bar, Tabs, Toolbar, etc.) will be created in Sprint-003A. All work is strictly backend domain models, protocols, profile manager, session manager, URL normalization, browser service, security policy, and storage infrastructure.

> [!NOTE]
> All existing 40 unit and UI tests will continue passing. Comprehensive unit tests for browser models, profile manager, session manager, and browser service will be added.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Browser Domain Models (`src/browser/models.py`)

#### [NEW] [src/browser/models.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/browser/models.py)
- Pydantic models (decoupled from Qt Widgets):
  - `BrowserSecurityLevel`: Enum (`STRICT`, `STANDARD`, `PERMISSIVE`).
  - `NavigationState`: Data model representing current URL, title, SSL status (`IS_SECURE`, `INSECURE`), loading progress, and back/forward availability.
  - `BrowserTabModel`: Data model representing a browser tab (ID, URL, title, icon, pin state, security state).
  - `BrowserProfile`: Data model representing profile metadata (profile_id, name, data_dir, cache_dir, cookies_dir, downloads_dir).
  - `BrowserSession`: Data model representing a saved session (session_id, workspace_id, open_tabs, active_tab_index, updated_at).

